1. Scope

This repository and the website published from it at https://voitiuk.com
contain several kinds of material:

- artworks, photographs, scans and artist-supplied materials;
- written and editorial content;
- structured data, metadata and the selection and arrangement of content;
- site-specific source code, visual design and other original modifications;
- third-party materials and portions of upstream software.

Except for third-party material and the upstream software described below,
these materials are protected by copyright and are not released under an
open-source or open-content licence. Making the repository or website publicly
accessible does not grant a licence to reproduce, distribute, republish,
modify or commercially exploit it.

2. Limited permissions

Without prior written permission, you may:

- access and display the public website in an ordinary web browser;
- link to its public pages;
- make temporary technical copies created automatically during normal browsing;
- view the public repository and use GitHub's built-in fork functionality only
  to the extent granted by GitHub's platform terms; this does not grant
  permission to deploy, publish, adapt or otherwise reuse the forked material;
- index public pages through a general-purpose search engine that respects
  robots.txt and does not republish the site's content; and
- quote short passages of text for criticism, review, news reporting, research
  or education when permitted by applicable law, provided that the author and
  a direct link to the source page are clearly identified.

These permissions do not include reproducing an entire artwork, image, page,
publication, dataset, collection or other substantial part of the website.

3. Uses requiring prior written permission

Except where applicable law expressly permits otherwise, you may not:

- copy, mirror, republish, distribute or make available all or a substantial
  part of the website or repository;
- reuse, download for republication, alter, sell or distribute artworks,
  photographs, scans, text, data or editorial material from the website;
- create a clone, derivative website or substantially similar presentation
  from the site-specific code, design, data or editorial arrangement;
- use the protected material commercially;
- perform bulk scraping or systematic downloading, other than the limited
  search-engine indexing described above;
- use the protected material to train, fine-tune, evaluate or supply a dataset
  for a machine-learning or artificial-intelligence system; or
- remove or obscure copyright, authorship or attribution information.

Nothing in this notice restricts quotation, accessibility, preservation or
other uses that cannot lawfully be excluded under applicable law.

4. Permission requests

For permission to reproduce or license material, use the contact form at:

https://voitiuk.com/en/contact/
